OneiOS, stack 555b13d (NativeMetal 935c468), patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0008: a client that may not write the same-user
shared cache directory keeps its cache across boots all the same.
Port of patches/NativeMetal/0017 (take20). The base changed what this is for: a client now tries first the same-user shared
directory (SharedShaderCache.h: ~/Library/Caches/org.unixnu.metal, i.e. /var/mobile/Library/Caches/org.unixnu.metal for
SpringBoard and the mobile daemons, and the render server takes the same one), which is kept across boots and shared between
the processes of the user, then its cache directory and its temporary directory. take20's folder
($HOME/Library/Caches/<its folder>/m2v) is tried between them: after the shared directory, before the directories the boot
empties, so it only serves a client whose sandbox refuses the shared one. A client that took a kept directory says which on
its text line (serial: `oneios-gpu-text: NAME[pid] cache Library/Caches/org.unixnu.metal`, or its own folder).
Switch: oneios-client-cache=temp (ONEIOS_CLIENT_CACHE=temp): take20's folder is not tried (the base's order alone; the shared
directory has the base's own switch, the environment variable NATIVE_METAL_SHARED_CACHE_DIR, empty = none).
Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=client-cache-kept-across-boots). Never compiled for iOS before this CI.

The header of the 624bab3 stack's patch (patches/NativeMetal/0017-client-cache-kept-across-boots.patch), which says the what and the why:
| OneiOS take20, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0017: a Metal client whose temporary directory is one the boot empties keeps its
| pipeline cache in its home's Library/Caches, so its pipelines are compiled once rather than at every boot.
| Upstream: none (OneiOS); the render server's own move of 2026 (marker 0x6814, ~/Library/Caches/com.apple.backboardd) for clients.
| What: clientDevice() first tries $HOME/Library/Caches/<folder>/m2v when confstr's temporary directory is under /private/var/mobile/tmp,
| /private/var/tmp or /tmp (each emptied by launchd's boot task dirs_cleaner); <folder> is the temporary directory's own folder there
| (com.apple.cameracaptured), else the bundle identifier (com.apple.springboard), else the process's name. Then the cache and
| temporary directories as before. A home of /var/empty, a missing Library/Caches or a folder the process may not make or write (a
| sandbox) leaves the earlier order. An app's container tmp/m2v (kept across boots) is not moved.
| Why: take19's Data store (data-take19.img, newest checkpoint) against take18's: /var/mobile/tmp/m2v (SpringBoard's RenderBox
| pipelines, 10:37:56-58 UTC) and /var/mobile/tmp/com.apple.cameracaptured/m2v (52 entries, as many as take18's) were written anew at
| take19's boot; take18's held 214 and 52, all written in take18's own session. Clients' confstr cache directory is empty on iOS, so
| every client took its temporary directory. The render server's cache is persistent and was hit at boot (take19: 52 build entries and
| 92 driver records read, the rest of its 1670 take18 entries untouched since).
| Risk: low. A sandbox that refuses the folder keeps the earlier order; the first boot with the patch compiles the moved clients'
| pipelines once into the new folder (what every boot did before). Disk: what those clients' caches hold (take19: about 100 entries).
| Switch: boot argument oneios-client-cache=temp (ONEIOS_CLIENT_CACHE=temp, Switches.inc): the earlier order. Default: on.
| Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=client-cache-kept-across-boots).
| iOS's serial log: `oneios-gpu-text: SpringBoard[32] cache Library/Caches/com.apple.springboard/m2v` (each client that took the
| folder, once); the Data store after the session: no new files in /var/mobile/tmp/*/m2v, the clients' folders under
| /var/mobile/Library/Caches; at the next boot those folders' entries are read (their access times move), not written again.

